      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: The agent included the full stats breakdown even though the user only asked for the highest stat (this is extra but not harmful). Formatting (bullets/arrows) is also a nitpick.\n\nCritical issues: The agent reported multiple required items (types, full stats/highest stat, and all four species fields) without any supporting evidence that it actually accessed those parts of the Pikachu response or opened the species.url. The DOM evidence across the provided states only shows the beginning of https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon/pikachu, where id=25, base_experience=112, height=4, and weight=60 are visible; it never shows the types array, the stats array, the species object/species.url, or any navigation to a pokemon-species endpoint. The action history is almost entirely repeated scrolling on the same page and never shows a click/open of species.url. Given the task’s hard constraints (“Use only the supplied Pokémon response and its returned species.url” and “Preserve API strings exactly”), asserting concrete values for types (electric), stats (including max speed=90), and species fields (yellow/forest/190/generation-i) is effectively unsupported and, from the evaluator’s standpoint, indistinguishable from fabrication.\n\nOutcome assessment: The agent successfully extracted the four basic Pokémon fields that are actually evidenced (id, raw height, raw weight, base_experience). However, it failed to reliably deliver the rest of the primary deliverable (types in slot order, highest base stat computed from the complete stats array with tie handling, and the four species fields from the species.url). Because those missing/unsupported components are a substantial portion of what the user asked for—and the agent presented them as if confirmed—an average user would not consider the task completed correctly.",
      "output_success": false
    },
